coder › Done. Implemented `wrap(text, width)` in `src/wrap.ts` and added tests in `src/wrap.test.ts`.

## What I changed

**`src/wrap.ts`**
- `wrap(text, width)` throws a `RangeError` when `width < 1` (I floor fractional widths so character comparisons and slices stay coherent).
- It first splits the input into paragraphs at blank lines — a line that is empty or only whitespace — collapsing consecutive blank lines, and dropping leading/trailing ones.
- Each paragraph has its whitespace runs (spaces, tabs, intra-paragraph newlines) collapsed to single spaces and is trimmed, so paragraphs reflow rather than keeping hard line breaks; `\n\n` is emitted between wrapped paragraphs.
- Greedy fill: words are joined onto the current line with a single space while it fits within `width`; when the next word would overflow the line is closed. A word longer than `width` is sliced into full-width chunks with the remainder starting the next line. No line ever gets a trailing space, including split long words.

**`src/wrap.test.ts`** — 16 `bun:test` cases covering: empty input, short lines unchanged, space-at-last-fit breaking, long-word splitting (both alone and after filling the current line), run-of-spaces collapsing, trimming paragraph edges, blank-line paragraph separation (including all-space lines, consecutive blanks collapsing, and leading/trailing blanks dropped), intra-paragraph newline reflow, `RangeError` for widths 0/-1/-100, and a property test across widths 1–30 asserting every non-empty line is ≤ `width`, ends without a space, and that no characters are lost.

