## Decisions the spec didn't spell out

- A "blank line" is any line that is empty or contains only whitespace.
- Consecutive blank lines in the input collapse to one separator; leading/trailing blank lines produce no empty lines at the edges of the output.
- Newlines *inside* a paragraph (non-blank) are treated as whitespace like spaces, so the paragraph reflows — the only preserved structure is blank-line paragraph separation.
- Character count treats `width` as whole characters (code units); fine for the ASCII scope here.

